BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Train to Busan in 4K with Yeon Sang-ho
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
DTSTAMP:20260816T082840Z
UID:019e0a0b-adbd-3b4f-a93e-c94024d83aed@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: director Yeon Sang-ho\n\nSaturday\, August 15\, 202
 6\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 58m\n\n201
 6 | 118 min. | Korea | Color | Korean | Not Rated | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED/WRIT
 TEN BY: Yeon Sang-ho \nWITH: Gong Yoo\, Jung Yu-mi\, Ma Dong-seok\, Kim Su
 -an\n\nType: Screenings\n\nWith the South Korean peninsula in the throes o
 f a national disaster\, travelers board the KTX\, a fast a train to Busan\
 , a city unaffected by the crisis. Among them is Seok-woo\, a workaholic f
 ather traveling with his daughter. When a young woman\, scuffed and dazed\
 , gets on board\, an unimaginable horror erupts in the train’s claustrop
 hobic confines. Director Yeon Sang-ho\, whose prior filmmaking comprises g
 roundbreaking animated features\, balances an upbeat\, kinetic energy with
  solid emotional storytelling to deliver much more than just an action-dri
 ven genre film.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/train-to-busan-019e0a
 0b-adbd-3b4f-a93e-c94024d83aed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Ugly with Yeon Sang-ho and Park Jeong-min
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
DTSTAMP:20260816T082840Z
UID:019e0a0a-e285-aa70-93a8-d960d2b0c160@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: director Yeon Sang-ho and actor Park Jeong-min\n\nS
 aturday\, August 15\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\
 n\nRuntime: 1h 43m\n\n2025 | 103 min. | Korea | Color | Korean | Rated R |
  DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Yeon Sang-ho \nWRITTEN BY: Yeon Sang-ho.\nWITH: Park 
 Jeong-min\, Kwon Hae-hyo\, Shin Hyun-bin\, Han Ji-hyun\n\nType: Screenings
 \n\nStarring in Yeon Sang-ho’s intimate suspense drama is Park Jeong-min
 \, in his compelling portrayal of Dong-hwan and the younger version of his
  father\, Yeong-gyu\, in flashback sequences. Yeong-gyu\, who cannot see\,
  is a renowned wooden seal carver\, respected for his intricate craftsmans
 hip. Dong-hwan has no memory of his mother\, who has been missing for 40 y
 ears—or so he’s been told—until he receives a startling call about h
 er remains. Adapted from his own graphic novel\, Yeon excavates the ugly a
 spects of societal standards and perceptions of beauty\, and unapologetica
 lly exhibits the dark sides of human greed\, desire\, and trauma.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-ugly-019e0a0a-e28
 5-aa70-93a8-d960d2b0c160
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Scooby-Doo in 35mm
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
DTSTAMP:20260816T082840Z
UID:019db103-7ebb-e23a-c52a-b153e188f713@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, August 15\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Mot
 ion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 26m\n\n2002 | 86 min. | USA | Color | English 
 | Rated PG | 35mm \nDIRECTED BY: Raja Gosnell \nWRITTEN BY: James Gunn 
 \nSTORY BY: Craig Titley\, James Gunn\nWITH: Freddie Prinze Jr.\, Sarah Mi
 chelle Gellar\, Matthew Lillard\, Linda Cardellini\n\nType: Screenings\n\n
 The Mystery Inc. gang from Hanna-Barbera’s classic cartoon\, Scooby-Doo\
 , Where Are You! took their sleuthing skills to the big screen with their 
 first live-action adventure in 2002’s Scooby-Doo. Led by ‘90s teen hea
 rtthrobs and real-life couple Freddie Prinze Jr. and Sarah Michelle Gellar
  as Fred and Daphne\, the amateur detectives Velma (Linda Cardellini)\, Sh
 aggy (Matthew Lillard) and his best friend\, the cowardly\, always hungry\
 , and vocal Great Dane\, Scooby-Doo\, reunite to solve the mystery of ghos
 tly happenings at the tropical resort Spooky Island. From a script co-writ
 ten by James Gunn and featuring Rowan Atkinson as the eccentric resort-own
 er\, the film was a box office success on its release and continues to hav
 e an avid following.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/scooby-doo-019db103-7
 ebb-e23a-c52a-b153e188f713
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Munich in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260816T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260816T160000
DTSTAMP:20260816T082840Z
UID:019d8804-e004-8e70-0ae5-e53d81175bb7@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, August 16\, 2026 at 2 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum 
 of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 47m\n\n2005 | 167 min. | USA | Color | S
 cope | English/German/French/Hebrew | Rated R | 35mm \nDIRECTED BY: Steven
  Spielberg \nWRITTEN BY: Tony Kushner\, Eric Roth \nWITH: Eric Bana\, Dani
 el Craig\, Ciaran Hinds\, Geoffrey Rush\nPrint courtesy of the Academy Fil
 m Archive.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nAfter the killing of Israeli hostages at
  the 1972 Summer Olympics in Munich\, a Mossad agent (Eric Bana) assembles
  a team to assassinate the men deemed responsible for the murders. Steven 
 Spielberg’s fact-based international thriller is a thoughtful look at th
 e moral costs of violence\, with gripping suspense and an impressive suppo
 rting cast including Best Actor winner Geoffrey Rush (Shine\, 1996)\, Supp
 orting Actor nominee Ciarán Hinds (Belfast\, 2021)\, and Daniel Craig\, s
 hortly before he debuted as James Bond. The film received five Oscar nomin
 ations including Best Picture\, Directing\, and\, for John Williams’ mus
 ic\, his 22nd feature score for the director. Williams’s somber\, restra
 ined score focused on\, in the composer’s words\, “the enormous suffer
 ing and guilt\, and eventually\, paranoia” of Bana’s protagonist.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/munich-019d8804-e004-
 8e70-0ae5-e53d81175bb7
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ponyo in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260817T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260817T150000
DTSTAMP:20260816T082840Z
UID:019dd51f-43b5-e687-8774-0d5f81c04a9c@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, August 17\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Muse
 um of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 43m\n\n2008 | 103 min. | Japan | Colo
 r | Japanese with English subtitles| Rated G | 35mm\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: 
 Hayao Miyazaki \nWITH: Tomoko Yamaguchi\, Kazushige Nagashima\, Yuki Amam
 i\, George Tokoro \nNew subtitled print courtesy of the Academy Film Arch
 ive\, with special thanks to Studio Ghibli.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nPonyo f
 ocuses on the friendship between 5-year-old Sosuke and a magical goldfish 
 named Brunhilde\, the young daughter of a sorcerer father and a sea-goddes
 s mother. After wandering away from her father’s four-flippered submarin
 e\, Brunhilde washes ashore and is discovered by the curious Sosuke. Now r
 enamed Ponyo\, she forms a quick bond with Sosuke that fuels her yearning 
 to be a real girl\, and together they shoulder the cost of what that might
  take. The vibrant and colorful hand-drawn animations are a delight for au
 diences of all ages\, as Hayao Miyazaki builds a world filled with magical
  goldfish\, spellcasters\, and sea goddesses in this tale of how friendshi
 ps can blossom anywhere—even in the ocean’s depths.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/ponyo-019dd51f-43b5-e
 687-8774-0d5f81c04a9c
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Snake of June
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260817T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260817T223000
DTSTAMP:20260816T082840Z
UID:019dd58f-be6b-74f3-d4b0-11084892d642@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, August 17\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Muse
 um of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 17m\n\n2002 | 77 min. | Japan | Color
  | Japanese with English subtitles | Rated R | DCP \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY:
  Shinya Tsukamoto \nWITH: Asuka Kurosawa\, Yuji Kotari\, Shinya Tsukamoto
 \, Susumu Terajima\n\nType: Screenings\n\nRinko Tatsumi (Asuka Kurosawa) i
 s a suicide hotline worker resigned to a life of unhappiness until she rec
 eives a package from a blackmailer. Through the increasingly vulgar acts o
 f exhibitionism her blackmailer forces upon her\, she learns to shed the s
 ocial restrictions and repression dominating her life. Shot on black-and-w
 hite film and tinted a monochromatic blue\, Shinya Tsukamoto’s A Snake o
 f June is a visual feast. Filled with shaky\, hand-held camerawork\, voyeu
 ristic close-ups\, and near-constant rain\, Tsukamoto creates a damp and c
 old erotic thriller that explores sexual dynamics\, transformation\, and r
 eleasing one's inner desires.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/a-snake-of-june-019dd
 58f-be6b-74f3-d4b0-11084892d642
END:VEVENT
