BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gunfight at the O.K. Corral in VistaVision
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260821T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260821T223000
DTSTAMP:20260816T082840Z
UID:019de50d-75de-011b-6835-d2abcb4adec8@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: actor Peter Weller\n\nFriday\, August 21\, 2026 at 
 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 2m\n
 \n1957 | 122 min. | USA | Color | English | VistaVision \nDIRECTED BY: Joh
 n Sturges \nWRITTEN BY: Leon Uris \nWITH: Burt Lancaster\, Kirk Douglas\, 
 Rhonda Fleming\, Jo Van Fleet\n\nType: Screenings\n\nJohn Sturges (The Mag
 nificent Seven\, 1960) directed this vivid re-telling of the classic Weste
 rn set in 1880s Arizona. Burt Lancaster is Marshal Wyatt Earp\, who partne
 rs with his brothers to clean up the town of Tombstone. Helped by loyal fr
 iend Doc Holliday (Kirk Douglas)\, they find themselves embroiled in a dea
 dly conflict with the Clanton family. The second film to team Lancaster an
 d Douglas\, Gunfight was nominated for its film editing and sound recordin
 g and features a rousing score by four-time Oscar winner Dimitri Tiomkin (
 High Noon\, 1952)\, with a memorable title song performed by Frankie Laine
 . In 1967\, Sturges continued the story with Hour of the Gun\, starring Ja
 mes Garner as Earp and Jason Robards as Holliday.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/gunfight-at-the-o-k-c
 orral-in-vista-vision-019de50d-75de-011b-6835-d2abcb4adec8
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nancy Drew
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T121500
DTSTAMP:20260816T082840Z
UID:019db103-fddd-6a12-cf78-c41fe1e4486c@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, August 22\, 2026 at 11 am\n\nLocation: Academy Muse
 um of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 37m\n\n2007 | 97 min. | USA | Color |
  Scope | English | Rated PG | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Andrew Fleming \nWRITTEN
  BY: Andrew Fleming\, Tiffany Paulsen \nSTORY BY: Tiffany Paulsen \nWITH: 
 Emma Roberts\, Josh Flitter\, Max Thieriot\, Tate Donovan\n\nType: Screeni
 ngs\n\nEmma Roberts steps into the role of Nancy Drew in this contemporary
  adaptation of the iconic teen detective. When Nancy’s father (Tate Dono
 van) gets a job that moves them to Los Angeles\, he encourages her to beha
 ve like an average teenager and refrain from sleuthing. Unable to refrain 
 from her passion\, Nancy dives into a famous cold case involving the death
  of a movie star. The subject of hundreds of novels\, and numerous film\, 
 television and video game adaptations\, the character of Nancy Drew has be
 en inspiring young women since the 1930s.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/nancy-drew-019db103-f
 ddd-6a12-cf78-c41fe1e4486c
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Ten Commandments in VistaVision
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T133000
DTSTAMP:20260816T082840Z
UID:019de50f-21df-5b2b-aa64-3ac6e6d9ce9e@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: Charlotte Barker\, senior director\, film preservat
 ion and restoration\, Paramount Archives\; and Craig Barron\, executive c
 reative director\, Magnopus\n\nSaturday\, August 22\, 2026 at 12 pm\n\nLoc
 ation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 3h 39m\n\n1956 | 219 
 min | USA | Color | English | Rated G | VistaVision \nDIRECTED BY: Cecil 
 B. DeMille \nWRITTEN BY: Aeneas MacKenzie\, Jesse Lasky Jr.\, Jack Gariss
 \, Fredric M. Frank \nWITH: Charlton Heston\, Yul Brynner\, Anne Baxter\,
  Edward G. Robinson\n\nType: Screenings\n\nThe final film directed by bloc
 kbuster master Cecil B. DeMille is a lavish remake of his own 1923 silent 
 epic. Charlton Heston\, as Moses\, leads a stellar cast\, including Yul Br
 ynner as Pharaoh Rameses II\, Anne Baxter as the lustful Nefretiri\, and E
 dward G. Robinson as the rebellious Dathan. The film was nominated for sev
 en Oscars\, including Best Picture\, and John Fulton (The Invisible Man\, 
 1933) won for its special effects\, which included such classic Biblical s
 equences as the Burning bush\, the Ten Plagues\, and the parting of the Re
 d Sea.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-ten-commandments-
 in-vista-vision-019de50f-21df-5b2b-aa64-3ac6e6d9ce9e
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Evening with Charlize Theron Featuring Mad Max: Fury Road
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T213000
DTSTAMP:20260816T082840Z
UID:019f24e4-20c3-8b06-55f7-05f9a1187e85@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Conversations,Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Charlize Theron engages in conversation with members of the Ac
 ademy Museum Teen Council before a special screening of Mad Max: Fury Road
  (2015).\n\nSaturday\, August 22\, 2026 at 7 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museu
 m of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h\n\nSchedule\n7pm | Conversation \n7:4
 0pm | Screening\n2015 | 120 min. | Australia | Color | Scope | English | D
 CP \nDIRECTOR: George Miller\nWRITTEN BY: George Miller\, Brendan McCarthy
 \, Nico Lathouris\nWITH: Tom Hardy\, Charlize Theron\, Nicholas Hoult\, Hu
 gh Keays-Byrne\n\nType: Conversations\, Screenings\n\nGeorge Miller return
 ed to the memorable post-apocalyptic world he created for Mad Max with thi
 s nonstop thrill ride that introduced a new Max (Tom Hardy) as well as a m
 emorable action heroine (Charlize Theron as Imperator Furiosa). The film r
 eceived 10 nominations including Best Picture and Directing\, and earned O
 scars for Costume Design\, Film Editing\, Makeup and Hairstyling\, Product
 ion Design\, Sound Editing\, and Sound Mixing.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/an-evening-with-charl
 ize-theron-featuring-mad-max-fury-road-019f24e4-20c3-8b06-55f7-05f9a1187e8
 5
END:VEVENT
