UID:019f1fdb-7bb1-0d3a-96fc-ec6cc22ce4f2@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Calling all creatures of the night: join the Academy Museum fo
 r a fang-tastic day exploring the vampire\, the most famous creature of th
 e dark\, with special-effects demos\, thrilling tours\, monster appearance
 s\, and more.\n\nSaturday\, October 24\, 2026 at 11 am\n\nLocation: Academ
 y Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 30m\n\nAt a glance\n11am | Movi
 e | Hotel Transylvania (2012) | Ted Mann Theater\n11am–1:30pm | Special 
 effects makeup and hair demo | Grand Lobby  \n12:30–2:30pm | Vampire blo
 od SFX family workshop | Shirley Temple Education Studio | Lower Level 1\n
 1–5pm | Monster meet and greet | Grand Lobby  \n1:30\, 2:30\, and 3:30pm
  | The Horror Tours | Level 4\n2:30pm | Movie | Blade (1998) | Ted Mann Th
 eater \n4–5pm | Killer Fitness performance and dance-along | Grand Lobby
     \n7:30pm | Movie | Horror of Dracula (1958) | Ted Mann Theater \nMonst
 er Mash offers early access for Academy Museum members. Please check back 
 for ticket sale information.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nCalling all creatures 
 of the night: join the Academy Museum for a fang-tastic day of special-eff
 ects makeup demonstrations\, thrilling tours\, monster appearances\, movie
 s\, and activities—all exploring the vampire\, the famous creature of th
 e dark. Embrace this year’s theme with Dracula\, vampire hunters\, and a
  relaxing monster resort.  \nFree with the purchase of a general admission
  ticket. Museum admission is free for youth 17 and under. \nDetails\n11am 
 | Movie | Hotel Transylvania (2012) | Ted Mann Theater | Lower Level 2\nRa
 ted PG\n11am–1:30pm | Special effects makeup and hair demo | Grand Lobby
   \nA scary-good time with transformations by special effects makeup artis
 t Gabi Gonzalez\, hair stylist Johnny Villanueva\, and Academy Award winne
 r Howard Berger.\nGeneral admission ticket not required. Program may end e
 arly.  \n12:30–2:30pm | Vampire blood special effects family workshop | 
 Shirley Temple Education Studio | Lower Level 1\nGet mixed up in the world
  of horror makeup with a lesson on creating Hollywood-worthy vampire blood
 \, featuring tools used by real artists. All ages are welcome.\n1–5pm | 
 Monster meet and greet | Grand Lobby  \nMeet Universal Studios' classic mo
 vie monsters—Dracula\, the Bride of Frankenstein\, and Frankenstein's mo
 nster—for a can't-miss photo opportunity. It’ll be a scream.  \nGenera
 l admission ticket not required. Monsters meet for 30 minutes at a time.  
  \n1:30\, 2:30\, and 3:30pm | The Horror Tours | Level 4\nOpen the door an
 d peek inside—if you dare—with a museum educator on a 30-minute guide 
 tour of The Horror Show exhibition. Get a behind-the-scenes look at the re
 presentation of vampires and gothic horror in film\, and explore the produ
 ction processes for many horror classics.\nTours are limited to 25 people 
 and are first-come\, first-served. Please arrive at the meeting place on L
 evel 4 up to 10 minutes before the start time to secure your spot. General
  admission ticket required.   \n2:30pm | Movie | Blade (1998) | Ted Mann T
 heater | Lower Level 2\nRated R \n4–5pm | Killer Fitness performance and
  dance-along | Grand Lobby    \nA horror performance and dance-along\, whe
 re fitness meets fear. \n7:30pm | Movie | Horror of Dracula (1958) | Ted M
 ann Theater | Lower Level 2\nNot Rated \nMonster Mash offers early access 
 for Academy Museum members. Please check back for ticket sale information.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/monster-mash-019f1fdb
 -7bb1-0d3a-96fc-ec6cc22ce4f2
END:VEVENT
